---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Release & Transition Status | Governance Commons" description="GC v1.2.0 pins and RFC-0001 public-boundary transition status.">
  <section class="section white">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">GC v1.2.0</p>
      <h1>Release baseline and boundary transition</h1>
      <p>GC v1.2.0 is the current umbrella pinning record. It does not turn the umbrella into a monolithic specification, and it does not activate the accepted RFC-0001 public boundary.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="intro-grid">
      <article class="surface"><h2>Released specification pins</h2><p>Agent Dossier v1.1.0, Agent Matrix v1.4.0, and ONS v1.3.0 are the three released specification pins presented by the pending boundary model.</p></article>
      <article class="surface"><h2>Historical runtime pin</h2><p>The v1.2.0 manifest also pins APO v1.1.0. RFC-0001 reclassifies APO as a reference-runtime candidate; the historical manifest is not rewritten as though that transition had already been active.</p></article>
      <article class="surface"><h2>Outside the baseline</h2><p>Agent Team Protocol v0.1.0 is emerging pre-release work and is not included in GC v1.2.0.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="surface" style="margin-top:30px">
      <h2>RFC-0001 activation state</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accepted:</strong> 2026-10-01. A-1 through A-5 implementation is authorized.</li>
        <li><strong>Not active:</strong> activation still requires all G-1 through G-5 conditions to verify.</li>
        <li><strong>Known open:</strong> the Agent Dossier schemas are present at the repository's default GitHub Pages address, but the canonical governancecommons.org URLs return 404 because the custom domain is not bound; APO has not met A-1 provenance/drift requirements; Agent Matrix still references unreleased Agent Dossier v1.4.0 on current main.</li>
        <li><strong>Publication:</strong> Python governance-commons 0.2.0 is published. npm 0.2.0 is not present in the registry; npm 0.1.1 remains latest even though the workflow now uses Trusted Publishing/OIDC.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="actions" style="margin-top:24px">
        <a class="button primary" href="/conformance">Validation support</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/governancecommons/governance-commons/blob/main/releases/gc-v1.2.0.yaml">Release manifest</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/governancecommons/governance-commons/blob/main/rfcs/RFC-0001-public-boundary-model.md">RFC-0001</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
